  "term": "spongioblast",
  "definition": "In historical neuroembryology, a spongioblast is one of the early cells that differentiates from the neuroepithelium alongside neuroblasts. Unlike neuroblasts, which develop into nerve-cells, spongioblasts remain to form the supporting framework of nervous tissue.",
